# NetGrid Project-Specific Patterns

## Network Interface Handling
- Always filter out virtual interfaces: veth, br-, lo, tailscale, vmsgohere
- Use real-time system queries for interface information
- Handle cases where interfaces may disappear during execution
- Cache vendor lookup results to avoid repeated API calls

## Data Models
- Use dataclasses for network interface data structures
- Include all relevant fields: name, state, speed, MAC, IP addresses
- Make fields optional where appropriate (e.g., speed may not be available)
- Use proper typing for network-related fields (IPv4Address, IPv6Address)

## CLI Design
- Keep CLI interface simple and focused
- Use Click for command-line argument parsing
- Provide clear help text for all options
- Support filtering and sorting options
- Output should be clean, aligned tables

## Vendor Lookup System
- Implement caching for OUI database lookups
- Handle network failures gracefully
- Use appropriate HTTP status codes for error handling
- Consider rate limiting for external API calls

## Testing Network Code
- Mock system calls (psutil, netifaces) in tests
- Test interface filtering logic thoroughly
- Verify vendor lookup caching behavior
- Test error conditions (network failures, missing interfaces)

## Performance Targets
- Interface discovery: < 100ms
- Table formatting: < 50ms
- Overall response time: < 200ms
- Memory usage: < 10MB for typical interface counts

## Future-Ready Architecture
- Design for real-time updates (ncurses-style)
- Consider event-driven architecture for monitoring
- Plan for cross-platform compatibility
- Keep performance in mind for large numbers of interfaces
